<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Template for the published Flatpak channel's landing page.
     .github/workflows/flatpak.yml substitutes @PAGES_URL@ and @REPOSITORY@
     and writes the result to the gh-pages branch as index.html. Edit this
     file, never the generated one. -->
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>KyPost — Flatpak channel</title>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
      body {
        font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.6;
        max-width: 46rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem;
      }
      h1 { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
      .sub { opacity: 0.7; margin-top: 0; }
      pre {
        background: rgba(127, 127, 127, 0.14);
        padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
        border-radius: 6px;
        overflow-x: auto;
      }
      code { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; }
      footer { margin-top: 3rem; opacity: 0.7; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>KyPost</h1>
    <p class="sub">Relay-based email client for KDE Plasma and Plasma Mobile.</p>

    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>
      KyPost is distributed from its own Flatpak remote. Adding the remote
      (rather than installing a one-off bundle) is what makes
      <code>flatpak update</code> work.
    </p>
    <pre><code>flatpak remote-add --if-not-exists flathub https://flathub.org/repo/flathub.flatpakrepo
flatpak remote-add --if-not-exists kypost @PAGES_URL@/kypost.flatpakrepo
flatpak install kypost com.urlxl.mail</code></pre>
    <p>
      The Flathub remote is needed for the <code>org.kde.Platform</code>
      runtime KyPost builds against; the app itself is not on Flathub and
      never will be.
    </p>

    <h2>Update</h2>
    <pre><code>flatpak update com.urlxl.mail</code></pre>
    <p>Or just <code>flatpak update</code>, along with everything else.</p>

    <h2>Uninstall</h2>
    <pre><code>flatpak uninstall com.urlxl.mail
flatpak remote-delete kypost</code></pre>

    <h2>Verifying the signature</h2>
    <p>
      The repository is GPG-signed. The public key is embedded in the
      <a href="@PAGES_URL@/kypost.flatpakrepo">.flatpakrepo</a> file above, so
      the <code>remote-add</code> command installs it automatically and
      <code>flatpak</code> rejects anything not signed by it. The same key is
      also published separately as
      <a href="@PAGES_URL@/kypost.gpg">kypost.gpg</a>.
    </p>

    <footer>
      <p>
        Source and issue tracker:
        <a href="https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@">github.com/@REPOSITORY@</a>.
        Licensed GPL-3.0-only.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
